#. module: mail_send_cc_bcc
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_mail_send_cc_bcc
msgid ""
"=============================\n"
"Email Cc and Bcc in One Email\n"
"=============================\n"
"\n"
".. \n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! This file is generated by oca-gen-addon-readme !!\n"
"   !! changes will be overwritten.                   !!\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! source digest: sha256:49b0219952df7fe6712463cbdafe26ffa012a8b1b976f0f3cf73aaa3d3b9feff\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Alpha-red.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Alpha\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-AGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-BM1--de%2Fodoo--mail--cc--bcc-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/BM1-de/odoo-mail-cc-bcc/tree/20.0/mail_send_cc_bcc\n"
"    :alt: BM1-de/odoo-mail-cc-bcc\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3|\n"
"\n"
"Adds the field *Bcc* to the email composer and sends a message as **one\n"
"single email** to all its recipients.\n"
"\n"
"Odoo 20 has *Cc* in its composer, but no Bcc, and it still sends one\n"
"email per recipient: a message to two people leaves the server as two\n"
"emails. With this module\n"
"\n"
"- the composer has a line *Bcc* below *Cc*,\n"
"- the recipients in To, Cc and Bcc get the same single email, with the\n"
"  To and Cc recipients in its header, as any mail program would send it,\n"
"- nobody sees who got a blind copy: not the other recipients, and not\n"
"  portal users who look at the messages of their document,\n"
"- two or more customers in *To* also get one common email instead of one\n"
"  each.\n"
"\n"
"Sending invoices has its own dialog in Odoo, without Cc; the module\n"
"*Invoice Email Cc and Bcc* (``account_move_send_cc_bcc``), installed\n"
"automatically with Invoicing, adds *Cc* and *Bcc* there.\n"
"\n"
"Followers of the document and internal users in *To* keep the\n"
"notification of Odoo with the buttons of their group; nothing changes\n"
"for them.\n"
"\n"
"The version for Odoo 19 of this module adds Cc as well, with the field\n"
"names of Odoo 20: after an upgrade the Cc recipients of old messages are\n"
"kept.\n"
"\n"
".. IMPORTANT::\n"
"   This is an alpha version, the data model and design can change at any time without warning.\n"
"   Only for development or testing purpose, do not use in production.\n"
"   `More details on development status <https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status>`_\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Nothing to configure.\n"
"\n"
"Who gets the one common email:\n"
"\n"
"- every partner in Cc and Bcc, also internal users, and also users who\n"
"  read their notifications in Odoo instead of by email: a copy is a copy\n"
"  of the email. Who enters himself gets it, too;\n"
"- customers and other external partners in To.\n"
"\n"
"A message without Cc and Bcc is only sent as one email if it is a\n"
"message to customers (not a notification of Odoo), has at least two\n"
"external partners in To and fewer than 50 of them. From that number on\n"
"Odoo does not show the recipients of a message to each other, and\n"
"neither does this module.\n"
"\n"
"The common email has the language and the layout of its first external\n"
"recipient in To. It never carries the buttons Odoo shows to internal\n"
"users.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"- Open the full composer on a document, for example with *Send by Email*\n"
"  on a quotation or with *Send message* and the button *Open Full\n"
"  Composer* in the chatter.\n"
"- Click *Cc* next to the recipients: the lines *Cc* and *Bcc* appear.\n"
"  Enter the recipients and send. One email leaves Odoo.\n"
"\n"
"|The email composer with Cc and Bcc|\n"
"\n"
"- The message in the chatter lists every recipient with the state of the\n"
"  email; open it with the envelope next to the message.\n"
"- A reply to a message proposes its Cc recipients again. Blind copies\n"
"  are never proposed again.\n"
"\n"
"Other modules pass the copies to ``message_post()`` like the recipients:\n"
"\n"
"::\n"
"\n"
"   record.message_post(\n"
"       body=body,\n"
"       message_type=\"comment\",\n"
"       subtype_xmlid=\"mail.mt_comment\",\n"
"       partner_ids=to_partners.ids,\n"
"       partner_cc_ids=cc_partners.ids,\n"
"       partner_bcc_ids=bcc_partners.ids,\n"
"   )\n"
"\n"
".. |The email composer with Cc and Bcc| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BM1-de/odoo-mail-cc-bcc/20.0/mail_send_cc_bcc/static/description/composer.png\n"
"\n"
"Known issues / Roadmap\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"- Bcc and the one common email belong to a message on one document.\n"
"  Sending to several documents at once (mass mailing mode of the\n"
"  composer) knows the Cc of Odoo only and sends one email per recipient.\n"
"- The small message box of the chatter has the Cc of Odoo but no Bcc;\n"
"  open the full composer.\n"
"- A message scheduled for later is sent with its Bcc recipients; the\n"
"  form of the scheduled message does not show them.\n"
"- One email has one state: if it is sent, every recipient counts as\n"
"  notified. A partner without an email address is left out and marked as\n"
"  failed.\n"
"- Followers get their own notification as before. Its header does not\n"
"  name the recipients of the common email anymore.\n"
"\n"
"Changelog\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"20.0.1.0.0 (2026-11-19)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- Version for Odoo 20. Cc in the composer and on messages is part of\n"
"  Odoo 20 now; the module adds Bcc and the one common email.\n"
"\n"
"19.0.1.0.0 (2026-11-19)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- First version.\n"
"\n"
